WHAT THIS LICENCE DOES AND DOES NOT COVER

It covers the records: the factual fields this project collected, normalised and
published — names, slugs, listing URLs, install counts, ratings, release dates,
and the provenance attached to each.

It does not cover, and this repository does not republish, prose written by
extension authors: descriptions, changelogs, screenshots and marketing copy on a
marketplace listing belong to whoever wrote them. Those fields were dropped
during export rather than relicensed here.

Third-party names appear verbatim. They are facts about the ecosystem, not
claims of any relationship with their owners.

Install counts and ratings carry a source label saying how each number was
obtained. Where a number was measured by an outside party rather than published
by the marketplace, the label says `third-party-measured` and no supplier is
named — the classification is what a reader needs, and the relationship is not
ours to publish.
